% module-6-examples.l4: the history view
%
% The timeless Logical English twin of the contracts of an L4 file (module-6-examples.l4), written
% by the L4 translator (docs/migration/l4.md, step 3): the contracts read over a finished
% history of events. For each obligation the program says when it starts, its deadline
% and which events meet it, and four rules say how it ends: met, missed, or still
% open when the history stops. The same obligations, in the same words, as the LE for LPS twin in LPS2's
% examples/migration/l4/; each scenario expects what that twin's run ended with, which
% agrees with L4's evaluator.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program was written by a translator from a program of another
% system. It is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
% implied, including any warranty that it is accurate, complete or fit for a
% particular purpose. The translation may be wrong: check it against its source
% before relying on it. It is not legal, tax, insurance, financial or other
% professional advice. Its authors accept no liability for any loss or damage
% arising from its use.

